1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,079
Clutching their throat, unable to speak or breathe?

2
00:00:03,079 --> 00:00:04,410
An adult may be choking.

3
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:08,963
If they can cough, encourage them to keep coughing.

4
00:00:08,963 --> 00:00:10,666
That's the best way to clear it.

5
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:16,742
1 — If they can't cough, speak or breathe, call emergency services, or have someone call.

6
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:18,711
2 — Lean them forward.

7
00:00:18,711 --> 00:00:22,005
Give up to 5 firm back blows between the shoulder blades.

8
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:29,764
3 — Then up to 5 abdominal thrusts: fist just above the belly button, pull sharply in and up.

9
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:36,049
Keep alternating 5 back blows and 5 thrusts until the object comes out or help arrives.

10
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:39,414
If they become unresponsive, start CPR.

11
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:42,489
After abdominal thrusts, always see a doctor.
